AB  - INTRODUCTION: Tracheobronchoscopy allows endoscopic inspection and management of 
      the tracheobronchial system. MATERIAL: The recommendation was developed in 1997 
      and updated in 2004 and 2009. RESULTS: The recommendations comment on indications 
      and contra-indications, instruments, anesthesia and complications of endoscopic 
      tracheobronchoscopy. DISCUSSION: Rapid technical advances in endoscopy have led 
      to changes in indications for different procedures, especially as pertains to 
      rigid and flexible endoscopy. The recommendations are designed to provide 
      guidance for ENT and affiliated specialties for choosing and processing 
      instruments and sedation methods.
