LID - 10.1016/j.cvex.2015.04.004 [doi]
AB  - Endoscopy in nonhuman primates (NHPs) has resulted in improvements in research 
      and clinical care for more than 4 decades. The indications and procedures are the 
      same as in humans and the approach is similar to that in dogs, cats, and humans. 
      Selected procedures are discussed including rhinoscopy, tracheobronchoscopy, 
      upper gastrointestinal endoscopy, laparoscopy, and endoscopic salpingectomy. This 
      short overview provides practitioners with pragmatic elements for safe and 
      effective endoscopy in NHPs.
