TI  - Tracheal trauma in rhesus macaques (Macaca mulatta).
PG  - 45-48
LID - 10.1111/jmp.12550 [doi]
AB  - Tracheal disruption is a previously unreported complication of nonhuman primate 
      social trauma. Two cases were identified in rhesus macaques with subcutaneous 
      emphysema. These cases resolved with medical management and demonstrate that the 
      combined use of radiography and tracheoscopy allows rapid assessment and 
      diagnosis of tracheal trauma in nonhuman primates.
