TI  - Error traps and culture of safety in esophageal atresia repair.
PG  - 139-142
LID - S1055-8586(19)30054-X [pii]
LID - 10.1053/j.sempedsurg.2019.04.018 [doi]
AB  - Esophageal atresia (EA) repair has always been a source of immense professional 
      gratification for the pediatric surgeon. In many ways, this anomaly defines the 
      entire profession. Due to its rarity, there is an increased risk of inadvertent 
      events occurring during correction. This article describes some of the error 
      traps that may occur in attempting esophageal reconstruction and how they may be 
      avoided.
