PG  - 869-80
LID - 10.1016/j.cvsm.2009.05.001 [doi]
AB  - Flexible endoscopy is a valuable diagnostic approach to the upper and lower 
      respiratory tract, because it allows direct visualization and sample collection. 
      Techniques requiring a range of specialized equipment and varying levels of 
      experience have been developed to access and evaluate each anatomic region. 
      Familiarity with appropriate indications for each procedure and normal 
      appearance, cytology, and culture results from each region will enhance 
      diagnostic success.
