PG  - 1810-1
LID - S0003-4975(14)01627-0 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.athoracsur.2014.06.119 [doi]
AB  - Tracheal necrosis is a rare life-threatening phenomenon that most often occurs 
      after thyroid operations or prolonged intubation. Conservative treatment can be 
      one choice in extensive tracheal necrosis. We report the case of a 59-year-old 
      man, with tracheal necrosis that developed after pharyngolaryngectomy, that we 
      treated conservatively using hyperbaric oxygen therapy and antibiotic therapy. 
      The follow-up was assured by tracheobronchoscopy. A year after his discharge, the 
      trachea was totally healed.
