TI  - Pneumomediastinum and emphysema in a case of a soft bronchial foreign body 
      aspiration in a child. A case report.
PG  - 59-61
LID - 10.1016/S0030-6657(11)70629-1 [doi]
AB  - Foreign body aspiration is a frequent cause of hospitalization in pediatric ENT 
      units. Pneumomediastinum and subcutaneous emphysema are possible complications of 
      tracheobronchoscopy with foreign body removal, but it is rare, that the foreign 
      body causes the complications itself. The authors present a very rare case of a 
      soft bronchial foreign body aspiration in a child with such complications.
